<!--
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 setdef <kerrick@setdef.com>
  SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

  A Lota game's manifest, in place of the one fledge build android writes
  (Fledge's lib/fledge/templates/android/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml at
  v0.5.1), whose icon mark Fledge fills here too. It adds what
  love-android's manifest asks of the system for LÖVE's engine: OpenGL ES
  3.0, vibration, a full screen with no title bar, and no restart of the
  activity when the screen turns or a keyboard comes and goes.

  Android restarts the activity for any other change of configuration,
  and SDL then ends the game and exits the app, in love-android too
  (doc/contributors/upstream/014.md). So, unlike love-android, the
  activity also handles dark mode (uiMode), the font's size and weight
  (fontScale, fontWeightAdjustment), the app's language (locale, with
  layoutDirection, which a change of language also changes), and a
  change of the system's overlays (assetsPaths), which Android 12 and
  newer make when the wallpaper's colours change, and the display's
  density (density), which "Display size" in the settings changes. SDL's
  own manifest handles none of the last two. A game hears dark mode as
  Lota.themechanged and the language as Lota.localechanged. It hears
  nothing of a change of density, and keeps the scale it launched with,
  as in LÖVE, which reads the density once.

  Back reaches the game as the key escape, and then SDL closes the app,
  as in LÖVE. A game that decides what Back does itself adds, inside
  <application>:

    <meta-data android:name="SDL_ENV.SDL_ANDROID_TRAP_BACK_BUTTON" android:value="1" />

  and MainActivity then keeps Android 13 and newer from closing the app
  through predictive back, too.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.VIBRATE" />
    <uses-feature android:glEsVersion="0x00030000" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.touchscreen" android:required="false" />
    <application android:label="@string/app_name"@@ICON@@>
        <activity
            android:name="org.setdef.fledge.host.MainActivity"
            android:theme="@android:style/Theme.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen"
            android:configChanges="orientation|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|screenLayout|keyboard|keyboardHidden|navigation|uiMode|fontScale|fontWeightAdjustment|locale|layoutDirection|assetsPaths|density"
            android:launchMode="singleInstance"
            android:exported="true">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
